\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1.5}{\ignorespaces Variables Used in Hierarchical Risk Factor Construction. Variables are grouped into four categories reflecting distinct dimensions of financial risk: credit conditions, funding market stress, monetary policy stance, and broad market performance. Within each category, the first principal component is extracted via EMPCA before aggregation into the final composite index in the second stage of the hierarchical procedure.}}{17}{table.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
